{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AqepUu2LbvTnupd495911v","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"ceo-cost-transcripts.py — cost/token report derived from harness-native\n3\ttranscripts (``message.usage`` per assistant turn), NOT the audit log.\n4\t\n5\t## Why this exists (PLAN-186 W0, S339)\n6\t\n7\t``ceo-cost.py`` and ``budget-summary.py``'s audit-log rollup report\n8\t``$0.00`` over 30 days because the audit log is a *governance* log (spawns,\n9\tvetoes, edits, ceremonies) — it is not a token ledger. The real spend lives\n10\tin the harness-native transcripts under\n11\t``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/*.jsonl`` (the main/\"assento\" sessions) and\n12\t``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` (spawned\n13\tsub-agents, both plain Task-tool and Workflow rails). Each ``type ==\n14\t\"assistant\"`` record carries a full ``message.usage`` snapshot: fresh\n15\tinput, output, and prompt-cache read/write (split 5-minute / 1-hour TTL).\n16\t\n17\tThis is documented in ``docs/research/s339-orchestrator-study/\n18\t05-finops-routing.md`` (P0-1, §1, §Metodologia) — that report's own\n19\tscratchpad-local aggregator produced **$11,137.97** over 2026-08-03 →\n20\t2026-09-02. This script is the in-tree, tested, stdlib-only version of\n21\tthat instrument.\n22\t\n23\t``budget-summary.py`` already reads *some* native transcripts\n24\t(``_read_native_spawn`` / ``collect_native_spawns``, lines 920-1200) but\n25\tonly under ``<session>/subagents/**`` — it never reads the top-level\n26\t``<session>.jsonl`` files, so it is structurally blind to the \"assento\"\n27\t(main session) spend, which the S339 report measured at 71% of the total.\n28\tThis script reads BOTH trees and separates them.\n29\t\n30\t## Pricing contract\n31\t\n32\tDefault pricing is an EMBEDDED table (``_EMBEDDED_PRICING`` below),\n33\tsourced from the S339 report §1.2/§1.4, itself derived from\n34\t``docs/provider-pricing.md`` (primary table + cache-tier multipliers,\n35\tlines ~130-153) and ``budget-summary.py``'s\n36\t``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` (the per-model cache-read\n37\texceptions, mirrored below; every other model at 0.10x base; cache\n38\tWRITE is 1.25x base at the 5-minute TTL and 2.00x base at the 1-hour\n39\tTTL — these multipliers are a\n40\tstructural constant, not something ``cost-table.yaml`` carries).\n41\t\n42\t``--pricing PATH`` (default ``cost-table.yaml`` next to this script)\n43\tattempts to load base ``input_per_mtok`` / ``output_per_mtok`` rows from\n44\tthat file's mini-YAML ``models:`` block. Two cases:\n45\t\n46\t- **Format doesn't match at all** (file missing, unreadable, no\n47\t  ``models:`` section found, zero rows extracted): fall back to the\n48\t  fully embedded table wholesale. ``cost-table.yaml`` in this repo has\n49\t  NO cache-read/cache-write columns at all — this instrument's whole\n50\t  point is cache-aware pricing, so a table that cannot express that is,\n51\t  by construction, a format mismatch for this use case; the embedded\n52\t  table is the one that can.\n53\t- **Format parses AND the path is the untouched default**: rows load\n54\t  from the file, then the Owner-ratified corrections in\n55\t  ``_RATIFIED_OVERRIDES_FOR_DEFAULT_TABLE`` are layered on top — but\n56\t  ONLY where the parsed row actually DIFFERS from the ratified rate.\n57\t  As of ``b6dce78`` the in-tree ``cost-table.yaml`` already carries the\n58\t  ratified ``claude-sonnet-5`` $2/$10 row, so on the default path the\n59\t  correction is currently a NO-OP and ``source`` says so. An\n60\t  unconditional overwrite would be worse than useless: it would print\n61\t  \"ratified correction\" while correcting nothing, and the day the\n62\t  table is legitimately refreshed it would silently mask the new rate.\n63\t  An EXPLICIT ``--pricing`` path supplied by the caller is trusted\n64\t  as-is, with no correction at all — the caller opted into a specific\n65\t  pricing config on purpose.\n66\t\n67\tCache-read/write multipliers are ALWAYS the structural constants above,\n68\tregardless of which base table is in play, applied per-model (the\n69\t``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` exceptions act on cache read only).\n70\t\n71\t## Corpus contract\n72\t\n73\t- Dedup key: ``message.id`` when present (an API response's usage\n74\t  snapshot is identical across every content-block JSONL line the\n75\t  harness writes for that one message — thinking/text/tool_use blocks\n76\t  each get their own line, all carrying the SAME ``message.usage``);\n77\t  falls back to ``requestId`` + record ``uuid`` when ``message.id`` is\n78\t  absent. The S339 report's methodology names a\n79\t  ``(requestId, apiBlockIndex, message.id)`` key; ``apiBlockIndex`` was\n80\t  not observed in this harness version's on-disk schema, so the key\n81\t  degrades to what IS observed without inventing a field.\n82\t- Role: \"assento\" for non-sidechain assistant turns in a top-level\n83\t  ``<session>.jsonl``; \"subagent\" for every assistant turn under\n84\t  ``<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` regardless of its own\n85\t  ``isSidechain`` value (path-shape is the classifier, mirroring\n86\t  ``budget-summary.py``'s rail-by-path doctrine — the corpus has no\n87\t  reliable field for this). A sidechain turn inside a top-level file (not\n88\t  observed in this corpus, but not structurally impossible) is skipped\n89\t  rather than double-counted: any Task-tool sub-dispatch already has its\n90\t  own dedicated ``agent-*.jsonl``.\n91\t- Never touches ``iterations`` on a usage record (it double-counts\n92\t  retries — same exclusion the S339 report's methodology names).\n93\t- A JSON-parse failure on a candidate line is skipped and counted, never\n94\t  raised. An ``unresolved`` model id (not found in the active pricing\n95\t  table, after stripping a trailing ``[..]`` context-window suffix such\n96\t  as ``[1m]``) is bucketed and reported with its token totals — never\n97\t  silently priced at $0 as if it were a genuine zero-cost turn, and never\n98\t  guessed.\n99\t\n100\t## Routing invariant (PLAN-186 AC-13, S361)\n101\t\n102\tEVERY execution of this instrument also ASSERTS, from runtime data only,\n103\tthat the model a spawn was SERVED equals the model its call site DECLARED\n104\t(``transcript_rollup()['routing']``: the CLI report, the ``--json`` payload,\n105\tand ``collect()``/``render_block()`` for ``ceo-cost.py`` and\n106\t``budget-summary.py``). ADR-144:140 measured ``agent(..., {model})`` routing\n107\ton ONE harness build (n=2) and carries no forward guarantee; a proof taken\n108\tonce at land time cannot see the harness going back to ``inherit`` later.\n109\t\n110\t- DECLARED is the ``model`` key of the spawn's ``agent-<id>.meta.json``\n111\t  sidecar: what the call actually passed. It is never read from the text of\n112\t  a script (an instrument that predicts code from text does not converge).\n113\t  Absent or ``inherit`` means NO claim at the site: counted, never a\n114\t  violation.\n115\t- SERVED is ``message.model`` of the paired ``agent-<id>.jsonl``, never the\n116\t  agent's self-report, read through the SAME ``scan_files()``/``dedup()`` as\n117\t  the cost report -- with ONE difference: the served model is a fact of the\n118\t  TURN, not of its bill, so the routing read lifts the ``usage``\n119\t  requirement. A turn the cost report drops for want of ``usage`` (null,\n120\t  absent, empty) is still read here, and an assistant record that cannot be\n121\t  read at all is counted (INCONCLUSIVE), never silently skipped. Chunks of\n122\t  one message resolve to the TERMINAL chunk (highest ``output_tokens``; on a\n123\t  tie the LATER line in file order). A message whose chunks disagree about\n124\t  the model is counted in ``chunk_model_splits`` (informational) when the\n125\t  terminal chunk can be elected from complete information; if one of those\n126\t  chunks has NO ``output_tokens`` the terminal cannot be proven, it is\n127\t  counted in ``chunk_terminal_unprovable``, the group is EXCLUDED from the\n128\t  comparison (its guessed terminal can neither raise a violation nor vouch\n129\t  for the routing) and the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE -- never GREEN, and never\n130\t  RED on that group's account; a RED can only come from another group whose\n131\t  terminal is proven. ``<synthetic>`` is a harness pseudo-model and is\n132\t  ignored.\n133\t- EVERY string taken from a transcript or a sidecar is made printable where\n134\t  it enters the instrument (non-printable characters become ``?``): a model\n135\t  id, a session id, a label or an archetype name cannot forge a verdict line\n136\t  or drive a terminal in ANY renderer.\n137\t- A WINDOW decides first. A sidecar the check cannot trust (unreadable,\n138\t  refused, or a declaration it cannot classify) gates a window only if its\n139\t  spawn has a turn inside it; one from outside is counted as\n140\t  ``out_of_window`` and never reaches the verdict. The same holds record by\n141\t  record: an unreadable assistant record with a valid timestamp OUTSIDE the\n142\t  window leaves before it is counted; only what has no temporal position at\n143\t  all (a torn line, no timestamp) or sits inside the window can make the\n144\t  verdict INCONCLUSIVE, and where that makes a spawn's placement unprovable\n145\t  the check fails closed. The ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters stay\n146\t  corpus-wide.\n147\t- LABEL is the sidecar ``description`` (the Workflow ``label``; the native\n148\t  spawn's ``description``).\n149\t- ALIAS -> FAMILY, not alias -> id. ``opus|sonnet|haiku|fable`` are matched\n150\t  by FAMILY, derived from the fleet tables and never retyped; a full id is\n151\t  matched EXACTLY (a ``-YYYYMMDD`` date suffix is tolerated). A pinned\n152\t  alias -> id table was refused on evidence: on one harness the same\n153\t  ``sonnet`` was served as ``claude-sonnet-5`` and later as\n154\t  ``claude-sonnet-5-5``, so such a table is red the day the substrate\n155\t  re-points the alias and green over the very hole it has to see. The\n156\t  alias -> served pairs actually observed are PRINTED, never judged.\n157\t- SECOND PREDICATE (the AC-10 requirement named for whoever closes AC-13):\n158\t  a spawn whose archetype (``customAgentType``, else ``agentType``) is in\n159\t  ``VETO_FLOOR_ROLES`` must be served inside ``VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`` --\n160\t  MEMBERSHIP, never a family prefix -- declared or not. Both sets are\n161\t  imported from ``_lib.agent_frontmatter``, never retyped. Declared ==\n162\t  served is silent about the floor (``model: sonnet`` on a VETO spawn\n163\t  matches itself and is still a breach), which is why this is a second\n164\t  predicate and not a corollary of the first.\n165\t- Verdicts, worst first: RED (a violation), INCONCLUSIVE (something the\n166\t  check could not read or classify, named), VACUOUS (nothing was compared:\n167\t  a vacuous GREEN is refused), GREEN. The exit code stays 0 so the cost\n168\t  report is never broken by a routing finding; ``--assert-routing`` turns\n169\t  the verdict into a gate: 0 GREEN, 1 RED, 3 not proven (INCONCLUSIVE or\n170\t  VACUOUS). Out of scope, declared: the seat (no sidecar), spawns that\n171\t  declare nothing, an archetype that the sidecar does not record (the\n172\t  persona-injected ``general-purpose`` rail), and whether a site's\n173\t  ``model:`` is the RIGHT one for its task class (AC-3a / W1).\n174\t\n175\tPRE-REGISTERED DEATH CRITERIA -- fixed here before the first real run;\n176\tchanging any number is a plan amendment, never an edit in passing.\n177\t\n178\t  K-A (the detector dies: rebuild or retire it, never tune around it)\n179\t    K-A1 positive control: the synthetic pair in\n180\t         ``test_ceo_cost_transcripts.py`` (declared ``sonnet`` and served\n181\t         an Opus id is RED; declared == served is GREEN) must hold on every\n182\t         CI run. A control that stops biting kills the detector.\n183\t    K-A2 blindness: an execution over a window with >= 20 spawn sidecars\n184\t         and ``declared == 0``, in a window the operator knows contained\n185\t         spawns that passed ``model:``, means the sidecar schema drifted\n186\t         under the detector. It is blind until rebuilt against the new\n187\t         schema. (The ``sidecars`` / ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters\n188\t         are printed on every run so this is checkable from the output.)\n189\t    K-A3 noise: three DISTINCT violations (three different sidecars) each\n190\t         judged a FALSE POSITIVE of the predicate IN WRITING means the\n191\t         predicate that fired is re-scoped by an ADR or deleted. A TRUE\n192\t         positive is not noise: a deliberate below-floor probe, or a\n193\t         harness fallback that really served another model, stays RED for\n194\t         as long as its spawn is inside the window. There is deliberately\n195\t         no suppression list in this file.\n196\t  K-B (what a RED means: the lever, not the detector)\n197\t    K-B1 a MISMATCH (no served turn on the declared model) on a site that\n198\t         declares ``model:``, reproduced by ONE control spawn with the same\n199\t         declaration on the same harness build, means ``model:`` does not\n200\t         route on that build: the explicit sites of W1/AC-3a are inert\n201\t         there, ADR-144's measurement is amended, and the premise \"route\n202\t         builders by ``model:``\" is suspended until a build whose control\n203\t         passes.\n204\t    K-B2 one FLOOR_BREACH restarts, from zero, the PLAN-186 W3\n205\t         end-of-transition clock (\"one full wave with no floor violation\n206\t         registered by the permanent detector\").\n207\t\n208\tStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9. Read-only: this script writes nothing.\n209\t\"\"\"\n210\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n211\t\n212\timport argparse\n213\timport glob\n214\timport json\n215\timport os\n216\timport re\n217\timport sys\n218\timport time\n219\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n220\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n221\tfrom pathlib import Path\n222\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n223\t\n224\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n225\t# _lib.runtime_paths (read-only import — this script never edits it or\n226\t# budget-summary.py; it only consumes the single resolver per CLAUDE.md §4\n227\t# \"No file in the audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally\").\n228\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n229\t_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n230\t_REPO_ROOT = _SCRIPT_DIR.parent.parent  # .claude/scripts -> .claude -> repo root\n231\t_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\n232\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n233\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n234\t\n235\ttry:\n236\t    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\n237\texcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - resolver import must never crash the CLI\n238\t    _rp = None\n239\t\n240\t\n241\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n242\t# Pricing tables\n243\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n244\t\n245\t\n246\t# Executable definitions bind directly to this facade's globals, preserving\n247\t# monkeypatches on public/private names without mutating imported templates.\n248\tfrom _lib._cost_transcripts_parts import install as _install_parts\n249\t\n250\t_install_parts(globals(), (\n251\t    \"pricing\", \"records\", \"routing_helpers\", \"routing\", \"rollup\", \"cli\",\n252\t))\n253\t\n254\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n255\t    sys.exit(main())\n256\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383b699d-3190-4c1b-a4de-9afabb13d7c6","uuid":"01290b29-bad8-4603-9e7c-82bb493286b4","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:24:41.599Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"ceo-cost-transcripts.py — cost/token report derived from harness-native\ntranscripts (``message.usage`` per assistant turn), NOT the audit log.\n\n## Why this exists (PLAN-186 W0, S339)\n\n``ceo-cost.py`` and ``budget-summary.py``'s audit-log rollup report\n``$0.00`` over 30 days because the audit log is a *governance* log (spawns,\nvetoes, edits, ceremonies) — it is not a token ledger. The real spend lives\nin the harness-native transcripts under\n``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/*.jsonl`` (the main/\"assento\" sessions) and\n``~/.claude/projects/<slug>/<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` (spawned\nsub-agents, both plain Task-tool and Workflow rails). Each ``type ==\n\"assistant\"`` record carries a full ``message.usage`` snapshot: fresh\ninput, output, and prompt-cache read/write (split 5-minute / 1-hour TTL).\n\nThis is documented in ``docs/research/s339-orchestrator-study/\n05-finops-routing.md`` (P0-1, §1, §Metodologia) — that report's own\nscratchpad-local aggregator produced **$11,137.97** over 2026-08-03 →\n2026-09-02. This script is the in-tree, tested, stdlib-only version of\nthat instrument.\n\n``budget-summary.py`` already reads *some* native transcripts\n(``_read_native_spawn`` / ``collect_native_spawns``, lines 920-1200) but\nonly under ``<session>/subagents/**`` — it never reads the top-level\n``<session>.jsonl`` files, so it is structurally blind to the \"assento\"\n(main session) spend, which the S339 report measured at 71% of the total.\nThis script reads BOTH trees and separates them.\n\n## Pricing contract\n\nDefault pricing is an EMBEDDED table (``_EMBEDDED_PRICING`` below),\nsourced from the S339 report §1.2/§1.4, itself derived from\n``docs/provider-pricing.md`` (primary table + cache-tier multipliers,\nlines ~130-153) and ``budget-summary.py``'s\n``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` (the per-model cache-read\nexceptions, mirrored below; every other model at 0.10x base; cache\nWRITE is 1.25x base at the 5-minute TTL and 2.00x base at the 1-hour\nTTL — these multipliers are a\nstructural constant, not something ``cost-table.yaml`` carries).\n\n``--pricing PATH`` (default ``cost-table.yaml`` next to this script)\nattempts to load base ``input_per_mtok`` / ``output_per_mtok`` rows from\nthat file's mini-YAML ``models:`` block. Two cases:\n\n- **Format doesn't match at all** (file missing, unreadable, no\n  ``models:`` section found, zero rows extracted): fall back to the\n  fully embedded table wholesale. ``cost-table.yaml`` in this repo has\n  NO cache-read/cache-write columns at all — this instrument's whole\n  point is cache-aware pricing, so a table that cannot express that is,\n  by construction, a format mismatch for this use case; the embedded\n  table is the one that can.\n- **Format parses AND the path is the untouched default**: rows load\n  from the file, then the Owner-ratified corrections in\n  ``_RATIFIED_OVERRIDES_FOR_DEFAULT_TABLE`` are layered on top — but\n  ONLY where the parsed row actually DIFFERS from the ratified rate.\n  As of ``b6dce78`` the in-tree ``cost-table.yaml`` already carries the\n  ratified ``claude-sonnet-5`` $2/$10 row, so on the default path the\n  correction is currently a NO-OP and ``source`` says so. An\n  unconditional overwrite would be worse than useless: it would print\n  \"ratified correction\" while correcting nothing, and the day the\n  table is legitimately refreshed it would silently mask the new rate.\n  An EXPLICIT ``--pricing`` path supplied by the caller is trusted\n  as-is, with no correction at all — the caller opted into a specific\n  pricing config on purpose.\n\nCache-read/write multipliers are ALWAYS the structural constants above,\nregardless of which base table is in play, applied per-model (the\n``_CACHE_READ_MULTIPLIER_OVERRIDES`` exceptions act on cache read only).\n\n## Corpus contract\n\n- Dedup key: ``message.id`` when present (an API response's usage\n  snapshot is identical across every content-block JSONL line the\n  harness writes for that one message — thinking/text/tool_use blocks\n  each get their own line, all carrying the SAME ``message.usage``);\n  falls back to ``requestId`` + record ``uuid`` when ``message.id`` is\n  absent. The S339 report's methodology names a\n  ``(requestId, apiBlockIndex, message.id)`` key; ``apiBlockIndex`` was\n  not observed in this harness version's on-disk schema, so the key\n  degrades to what IS observed without inventing a field.\n- Role: \"assento\" for non-sidechain assistant turns in a top-level\n  ``<session>.jsonl``; \"subagent\" for every assistant turn under\n  ``<session>/subagents/**/agent-*.jsonl`` regardless of its own\n  ``isSidechain`` value (path-shape is the classifier, mirroring\n  ``budget-summary.py``'s rail-by-path doctrine — the corpus has no\n  reliable field for this). A sidechain turn inside a top-level file (not\n  observed in this corpus, but not structurally impossible) is skipped\n  rather than double-counted: any Task-tool sub-dispatch already has its\n  own dedicated ``agent-*.jsonl``.\n- Never touches ``iterations`` on a usage record (it double-counts\n  retries — same exclusion the S339 report's methodology names).\n- A JSON-parse failure on a candidate line is skipped and counted, never\n  raised. An ``unresolved`` model id (not found in the active pricing\n  table, after stripping a trailing ``[..]`` context-window suffix such\n  as ``[1m]``) is bucketed and reported with its token totals — never\n  silently priced at $0 as if it were a genuine zero-cost turn, and never\n  guessed.\n\n## Routing invariant (PLAN-186 AC-13, S361)\n\nEVERY execution of this instrument also ASSERTS, from runtime data only,\nthat the model a spawn was SERVED equals the model its call site DECLARED\n(``transcript_rollup()['routing']``: the CLI report, the ``--json`` payload,\nand ``collect()``/``render_block()`` for ``ceo-cost.py`` and\n``budget-summary.py``). ADR-144:140 measured ``agent(..., {model})`` routing\non ONE harness build (n=2) and carries no forward guarantee; a proof taken\nonce at land time cannot see the harness going back to ``inherit`` later.\n\n- DECLARED is the ``model`` key of the spawn's ``agent-<id>.meta.json``\n  sidecar: what the call actually passed. It is never read from the text of\n  a script (an instrument that predicts code from text does not converge).\n  Absent or ``inherit`` means NO claim at the site: counted, never a\n  violation.\n- SERVED is ``message.model`` of the paired ``agent-<id>.jsonl``, never the\n  agent's self-report, read through the SAME ``scan_files()``/``dedup()`` as\n  the cost report -- with ONE difference: the served model is a fact of the\n  TURN, not of its bill, so the routing read lifts the ``usage``\n  requirement. A turn the cost report drops for want of ``usage`` (null,\n  absent, empty) is still read here, and an assistant record that cannot be\n  read at all is counted (INCONCLUSIVE), never silently skipped. Chunks of\n  one message resolve to the TERMINAL chunk (highest ``output_tokens``; on a\n  tie the LATER line in file order). A message whose chunks disagree about\n  the model is counted in ``chunk_model_splits`` (informational) when the\n  terminal chunk can be elected from complete information; if one of those\n  chunks has NO ``output_tokens`` the terminal cannot be proven, it is\n  counted in ``chunk_terminal_unprovable``, the group is EXCLUDED from the\n  comparison (its guessed terminal can neither raise a violation nor vouch\n  for the routing) and the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE -- never GREEN, and never\n  RED on that group's account; a RED can only come from another group whose\n  terminal is proven. ``<synthetic>`` is a harness pseudo-model and is\n  ignored.\n- EVERY string taken from a transcript or a sidecar is made printable where\n  it enters the instrument (non-printable characters become ``?``): a model\n  id, a session id, a label or an archetype name cannot forge a verdict line\n  or drive a terminal in ANY renderer.\n- A WINDOW decides first. A sidecar the check cannot trust (unreadable,\n  refused, or a declaration it cannot classify) gates a window only if its\n  spawn has a turn inside it; one from outside is counted as\n  ``out_of_window`` and never reaches the verdict. The same holds record by\n  record: an unreadable assistant record with a valid timestamp OUTSIDE the\n  window leaves before it is counted; only what has no temporal position at\n  all (a torn line, no timestamp) or sits inside the window can make the\n  verdict INCONCLUSIVE, and where that makes a spawn's placement unprovable\n  the check fails closed. The ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters stay\n  corpus-wide.\n- LABEL is the sidecar ``description`` (the Workflow ``label``; the native\n  spawn's ``description``).\n- ALIAS -> FAMILY, not alias -> id. ``opus|sonnet|haiku|fable`` are matched\n  by FAMILY, derived from the fleet tables and never retyped; a full id is\n  matched EXACTLY (a ``-YYYYMMDD`` date suffix is tolerated). A pinned\n  alias -> id table was refused on evidence: on one harness the same\n  ``sonnet`` was served as ``claude-sonnet-5`` and later as\n  ``claude-sonnet-5-5``, so such a table is red the day the substrate\n  re-points the alias and green over the very hole it has to see. The\n  alias -> served pairs actually observed are PRINTED, never judged.\n- SECOND PREDICATE (the AC-10 requirement named for whoever closes AC-13):\n  a spawn whose archetype (``customAgentType``, else ``agentType``) is in\n  ``VETO_FLOOR_ROLES`` must be served inside ``VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`` --\n  MEMBERSHIP, never a family prefix -- declared or not. Both sets are\n  imported from ``_lib.agent_frontmatter``, never retyped. Declared ==\n  served is silent about the floor (``model: sonnet`` on a VETO spawn\n  matches itself and is still a breach), which is why this is a second\n  predicate and not a corollary of the first.\n- Verdicts, worst first: RED (a violation), INCONCLUSIVE (something the\n  check could not read or classify, named), VACUOUS (nothing was compared:\n  a vacuous GREEN is refused), GREEN. The exit code stays 0 so the cost\n  report is never broken by a routing finding; ``--assert-routing`` turns\n  the verdict into a gate: 0 GREEN, 1 RED, 3 not proven (INCONCLUSIVE or\n  VACUOUS). Out of scope, declared: the seat (no sidecar), spawns that\n  declare nothing, an archetype that the sidecar does not record (the\n  persona-injected ``general-purpose`` rail), and whether a site's\n  ``model:`` is the RIGHT one for its task class (AC-3a / W1).\n\nPRE-REGISTERED DEATH CRITERIA -- fixed here before the first real run;\nchanging any number is a plan amendment, never an edit in passing.\n\n  K-A (the detector dies: rebuild or retire it, never tune around it)\n    K-A1 positive control: the synthetic pair in\n         ``test_ceo_cost_transcripts.py`` (declared ``sonnet`` and served\n         an Opus id is RED; declared == served is GREEN) must hold on every\n         CI run. A control that stops biting kills the detector.\n    K-A2 blindness: an execution over a window with >= 20 spawn sidecars\n         and ``declared == 0``, in a window the operator knows contained\n         spawns that passed ``model:``, means the sidecar schema drifted\n         under the detector. It is blind until rebuilt against the new\n         schema. (The ``sidecars`` / ``declared`` / ``undeclared`` counters\n         are printed on every run so this is checkable from the output.)\n    K-A3 noise: three DISTINCT violations (three different sidecars) each\n         judged a FALSE POSITIVE of the predicate IN WRITING means the\n         predicate that fired is re-scoped by an ADR or deleted. A TRUE\n         positive is not noise: a deliberate below-floor probe, or a\n         harness fallback that really served another model, stays RED for\n         as long as its spawn is inside the window. There is deliberately\n         no suppression list in this file.\n  K-B (what a RED means: the lever, not the detector)\n    K-B1 a MISMATCH (no served turn on the declared model) on a site that\n         declares ``model:``, reproduced by ONE control spawn with the same\n         declaration on the same harness build, means ``model:`` does not\n         route on that build: the explicit sites of W1/AC-3a are inert\n         there, ADR-144's measurement is amended, and the premise \"route\n         builders by ``model:``\" is suspended until a build whose control\n         passes.\n    K-B2 one FLOOR_BREACH restarts, from zero, the PLAN-186 W3\n         end-of-transition clock (\"one full wave with no floor violation\n         registered by the permanent detector\").\n\nStdlib-only, Python >= 3.9. Read-only: this script writes nothing.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport glob\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# _lib.runtime_paths (read-only import — this script never edits it or\n# budget-summary.py; it only consumes the single resolver per CLAUDE.md §4\n# \"No file in the audit/state family may re-derive the directory locally\").\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n_SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n_REPO_ROOT = _SCRIPT_DIR.parent.parent  # .claude/scripts -> .claude -> repo root\n_HOOKS_DIR = _REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n\ntry:\n    from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\nexcept Exception:  # pragma: no cover - resolver import must never crash the CLI\n    _rp = None\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Pricing tables\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n# Executable definitions bind directly to this facade's globals, preserving\n# monkeypatches on public/private names without mutating imported templates.\nfrom _lib._cost_transcripts_parts import install as _install_parts\n\n_install_parts(globals(), (\n    \"pricing\", \"records\", \"routing_helpers\", \"routing\", \"rollup\", \"cli\",\n))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":256,"startLine":1,"totalLines":256}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AqepUu2LbvTnupd495911v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
