{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1Q9NtMZmdGQ5xxc29cz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UGPiQ5pqjhoUyHgBzY7vR6","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/check-audit-real-loss.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4619,"cache_read_input_tokens":160594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4619},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383b699d-3190-4c1b-a4de-9afabb13d7c6","uuid":"023eb7ef-7b0b-4435-98d9-dd610a9a3915","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:28:03.323Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1Q9NexaLCXgfeDLhNSv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UGPiQ5pqjhoUyHgBzY7vR6":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/check-audit-real-loss.py"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGPiQ5pqjhoUyHgBzY7vR6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"check-audit-real-loss.py — G6 (real loss) and G7 (direct-writer loss), read-only.\n3\t\n4\tPLAN-194 W2 / ADR-055-AMEND-4 §8.2. Runs outside any hook (LAND V-block,\n5\tnightly, ``/ceo-boot``); ``--since`` is the LAND stamp.\n6\t\n7\t**G6.** A ``record_id`` with a ``commit`` envelope in a per-PID journal (or the\n8\taggregate journal) and ``wall_ns >= since`` that is neither in the canonical log\n9\tnor in a rotated archive nor in any spool-side file. Reading order, so a record\n10\tin transit is never called lost: (0) the journals; (1) a FRESH listing of the\n11\tspool side — active spools and ``.draining.*`` (PENDING) and the quarantine\n12\tfiles ``.malformed.*``/``.quarantined.*``/``.test-origin.*``/``.corrupt-header.*``\n13\t(QUARANTINED, never lost); (2) the canonical log through one descriptor; (3) the\n14\trotated archives, listed after it. A record only moves spool -> log (append\n15\tbefore unlink) and rotation renames the log. Log lines count by their TOP-LEVEL\n16\t``record_id``; a spool-side line that is not JSON (quarantine) is searched with\n17\t``_RID_RX``. Lower bound: a ``commit`` that never left the in-memory journal\n18\tbuffer, one whose journal compaction removed, or one TRUNCATED on disk (it is a\n19\tline that does not parse: only ``journal_malformed_lines`` sees it) is invisible.\n20\tHence ``attention`` (below).\n21\t\n22\tA pass of (1)-(3) is STABLE only if every listed spool-side file and archive was\n23\tread (none vanished between the listing and the read — a drain renames active\n24\t-> ``.draining``, a quarantine ``.draining`` -> ``.malformed``, a split writes a\n25\tnew ``.draining``) AND no ``.draining``/quarantine name shows up in a re-listing\n26\tthat the first listing missed (a rename caught mid-``readdir``). Where a record\n27\tIS seen counts in any pass; its ABSENCE counts only in stable passes. A loss is\n28\treported only after TWO stable passes; if ``MAX_PASSES`` run out first the\n29\tcandidates are ``unresolved`` and G6 is ``inconclusive`` (exit 2, never \"lost\").\n30\tA journal that vanishes is counted apart (``journals_vanished``): it can only\n31\tshrink the commit set, never create a loss.\n32\t\n33\t**G7.** ``audit_log`` lines (``[ts]`` stamp) ``lock timeout (stale?)  would-log=``\n34\tor ``append failed:`` in ``audit-log.errors`` stamped at or after ``since``. The\n35\tline parser reads BOTH stamp formats (``[AAAA-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ] ...`` of\n36\t``audit_log`` and ``AAAA-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ <writer>: ...``, §4.8 — the bare stamp is\n37\tshared by ``spool_writer``, ``audit_emit`` and ``check_budget``, so a class is\n38\tkeyed on the WRITER too) and also reports, never as G7, the ``STARVED`` lines (G8\n39\t``(exit)`` and the AMEND-3 opportunistic one) and ``drain canonical lock timeout``\n40\t(G2). A line with no stamp, or an impossible date, is counted as ``unparsed``.\n41\tThe ``STARVED (exit)`` text is the W2 form pinned by §4.3; until the W2 lands it\n42\texists only in the amendment and in the test fixture, so G8 reads 0 by design.\n43\t\n44\t``attention`` lists what the caller (``/ceo-boot``, nightly) must surface even\n45\tthough the exit code ignores it: ``g6_journal_malformed_lines`` — at least one\n46\tjournal line that does not parse, e.g. a truncated ``commit``, whose record G6\n47\tcannot follow.\n48\t\n49\tNames, resolver, refusal, streaming and read-only discipline come from\n50\t``audit_spool_state.py``. Exit: 0 clean; 1 G6 loss > 0 or G7 > 0; 2 usage,\n51\trefusal, unreadable input, or G6 inconclusive with nothing red. Stdlib only,\n52\tPython >= 3.9.\n53\t\"\"\"\n54\t\n55\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n56\t\n57\timport argparse\n58\timport json\n59\timport re\n60\timport sys\n61\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n62\tfrom pathlib import Path\n63\tfrom typing import Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n64\t\n65\t# These entries are read-only diagnostics.  Set this before loading the local\n66\t# verifier so a normal CLI invocation cannot create a cache beside its source.\n67\tsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n68\t\n69\tif str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent) not in sys.path:\n70\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n71\timport audit_spool_state as ss  # noqa: E402\n72\t\n73\tRE_QUARANTINE = (r\"audit-spool\\.([1-9][0-9]{0,9})\"\n74\t                 r\"\\.(?:malformed|quarantined|test-origin|corrupt-header)\\.([0-9a-f]{8})\")\n75\t_QUARANTINE_RX = re.compile(RE_QUARANTINE, re.ASCII)\n76\tAGGREGATE_JOURNAL = \"audit-pending.journal\"\n77\tERRORS_FILE = \"audit-log.errors\"\n78\tMAX_PASSES = 8\n79\t_RID_RX = re.compile(rb'\"record_id\"\\s*:\\s*\"([0-9a-f]{32})\"')\n80\t_STAMP = r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}Z\"\n81\tRE_ERR_LINE = r\"(?:\\[(%s)\\] |(%s) ([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*): )(.*)\" % (_STAMP, _STAMP)\n82\t_ERR_LINE_RX = re.compile(RE_ERR_LINE, re.ASCII)\n83\t# (class, source, message prefix); first match wins. Only the g7_* classes are G7.\n84\tERR_CLASSES = (\n85\t    (\"g7_would_log\", \"audit_log\", \"lock timeout (stale?)  would-log=\"),\n86\t    (\"g7_append_failed\", \"audit_log\", \"append failed:\"),\n87\t    # PLAN-194 W2.1: this text exists only in ADR-055-AMEND-4 §4.3 until W2.1 ships\n88\t    # its producer; then the G7 control drops the typed line for the real producer.\n89\t    (\"g8_starved_exit\", \"spool_writer\", \"drain canonical lock STARVED (exit)\"),\n90\t    (\"starved_opportunistic\", \"spool_writer\", \"drain canonical lock STARVED:\"),\n91\t    (\"g2_canonical_lock_timeout\", \"spool_writer\", \"drain canonical lock timeout\"),\n92\t)\n93\t\n94\t\n95\tdef _is_int(v: object) -> bool:\n96\t    return isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool)\n97\t\n98\t\n99\tdef record_ids(lines: Iterable[bytes], top_level_only: bool, wanted: Set[str],\n100\t               malformed_files: Optional[Set[str]] = None, source: str = \"\") -> Set[str]:\n101\t    \"\"\"The ``wanted`` ids among ``lines`` (memory follows the candidates, not the log).\"\"\"\n102\t    out: Set[str] = set()\n103\t    for line in lines:\n104\t        if b'\"record_id\"' not in line:\n105\t            continue\n106\t        try:\n107\t            e = json.loads(line)\n108\t        except ValueError:\n109\t            if not top_level_only:\n110\t                out.update(r for r in (m.decode(\"ascii\") for m in _RID_RX.findall(line))\n111\t                           if r in wanted)\n112\t            continue\n113\t        if not isinstance(e, dict) or \"record_id\" not in e:\n114\t            continue\n115\t        rid = e[\"record_id\"]\n116\t        if not isinstance(rid, str):\n117\t            if malformed_files is not None:\n118\t                malformed_files.add(source)\n119\t            continue\n120\t        if rid in wanted:\n121\t            out.add(rid)\n122\t    return out\n123\t\n124\t\n125\tdef journal_commits(st: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since_ns: int) -> Tuple[Set[str], int, int]:\n126\t    commits: Set[str] = set()\n127\t    malformed = 0\n128\t    vanished: List[str] = []\n129\t    for name in st.names():\n130\t        if name != AGGREGATE_JOURNAL and not ss.NAME_PATTERNS[\"journal\"].fullmatch(name):\n131\t            continue\n132\t        for line in ss.listed_lines(st, name, vanished):\n133\t            if not line.strip():\n134\t                continue\n135\t            try:\n136\t                env = json.loads(line)\n137\t            except ValueError:\n138\t                malformed += 1\n139\t                continue\n140\t            if (isinstance(env, dict) and env.get(\"op\") == \"commit\"\n141\t                    and isinstance(env.get(\"record_id\"), str)\n142\t                    and _is_int(env.get(\"wall_ns\")) and env[\"wall_ns\"] >= since_ns):\n143\t                commits.add(env[\"record_id\"])\n144\t    return commits, malformed, len(vanished)\n145\t\n146\t\n147\tdef _spool_side(name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n148\t    kind, _ = ss.classify(name)\n149\t    if kind in (\"active_spool\", \"draining\"):\n150\t        return \"pending\"\n151\t    return \"quarantined\" if _QUARANTINE_RX.fullmatch(name) else None\n152\t\n153\t\n154\tdef snapshot(fam: ss.ReadOnlyDir, st: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since_ns: int,\n155\t             wanted: Set[str]) -> Dict[str, Set[str]]:\n156\t    \"\"\"Steps (1)-(3) of the reading order, from fresh listings; ``unstable`` names\n157\t    the files that vanished before their read and the rename targets that appeared.\"\"\"\n158\t    snap: Dict[str, Set[str]] = {\n159\t        \"pending\": set(), \"quarantined\": set(), \"logged\": set(),\n160\t        \"malformed_record_id_files\": set(),\n161\t    }\n162\t    vanished: List[str] = []\n163\t    listed = {n: k for n, k in ((n, _spool_side(n)) for n in st.names()) if k}\n164\t    for name in sorted(listed):\n165\t        snap[listed[name]] |= record_ids(\n166\t            ss.listed_lines(st, name, vanished), False, wanted,\n167\t            snap[\"malformed_record_id_files\"], name,\n168\t        )\n169\t    for name, lines in ss.read_logs(fam, since_ns, vanished):\n170\t        snap[\"logged\"] |= record_ids(\n171\t            lines, True, wanted, snap[\"malformed_record_id_files\"], name,\n172\t        )\n173\t    appeared = [n for n in st.names() if n not in listed and _spool_side(n)\n174\t                and ss.classify(n)[0] != \"active_spool\"]  # never a rename target\n175\t    snap[\"unstable\"] = set(vanished) | set(appeared)\n176\t    return snap\n177\t\n178\t\n179\tdef g6(fam: ss.ReadOnlyDir, st: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since_ns: int) -> Dict[str, object]:\n180\t    commits, malformed, journals_vanished = journal_commits(st, since_ns)\n181\t    lost = set(commits)\n182\t    pending: Set[str] = set()\n183\t    quarantined: Set[str] = set()\n184\t    unstable: List[str] = []\n185\t    malformed_record_id_files: Set[str] = set()\n186\t    passes = stable = 0\n187\t    while lost and stable < 2 and passes < MAX_PASSES:\n188\t        passes += 1\n189\t        snap = snapshot(fam, st, since_ns, lost)\n190\t        malformed_record_id_files |= snap.get(\"malformed_record_id_files\", set())\n191\t        lost -= snap[\"logged\"]\n192\t        quarantined |= lost & snap[\"quarantined\"]\n193\t        lost -= snap[\"quarantined\"]\n194\t        pending |= lost & snap[\"pending\"]\n195\t        lost -= snap[\"pending\"]\n196\t        if snap[\"unstable\"]:\n197\t            unstable = sorted(snap[\"unstable\"])\n198\t        else:\n199\t            stable += 1\n200\t    inconclusive = bool(lost) and stable < 2\n201\t    ids = sorted(lost)[:50]\n202\t    return {\"commits\": len(commits), \"pending\": len(pending), \"quarantined\": len(quarantined),\n203\t            \"lost\": 0 if inconclusive else len(lost), \"lost_record_ids\": [] if inconclusive else ids,\n204\t            \"inconclusive\": inconclusive, \"unresolved\": len(lost) if inconclusive else 0,\n205\t            \"unresolved_record_ids\": ids if inconclusive else [], \"passes\": passes,\n206\t            \"stable_passes\": stable, \"last_unstable\": unstable[:20],\n207\t            \"journals_vanished\": journals_vanished, \"journal_malformed_lines\": malformed,\n208\t            \"malformed_record_id_files\": sorted(malformed_record_id_files)[:50]}\n209\t\n210\t\n211\tdef g7(fam: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since: datetime) -> Dict[str, object]:\n212\t    counts = {cls: 0 for cls, _, _ in ERR_CLASSES}\n213\t    counts.update(lines_in_window=0, unparsed=0)\n214\t    for line in ss.listed_lines(fam, ERRORS_FILE, []):\n215\t        raw = line.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\").rstrip(\"\\n\")\n216\t        m = _ERR_LINE_RX.fullmatch(raw)\n217\t        try:\n218\t            ts = datetime.strptime(m.group(1) or m.group(2), \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\") if m else None\n219\t        except ValueError:\n220\t            ts = None\n221\t        if ts is None:\n222\t            counts[\"unparsed\"] += 1 if raw else 0\n223\t            continue\n224\t        if ts.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) < since:\n225\t            continue\n226\t        counts[\"lines_in_window\"] += 1\n227\t        source = \"audit_log\" if m.group(1) else m.group(3)\n228\t        for cls, src, prefix in ERR_CLASSES:\n229\t            if src == source and m.group(4).startswith(prefix):\n230\t                counts[cls] += 1\n231\t                break\n232\t    counts[\"G7\"] = counts[\"g7_would_log\"] + counts[\"g7_append_failed\"]\n233\t    return counts\n234\t\n235\t\n236\tdef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n237\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"check-audit-real-loss.py\", description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n238\t    ap.add_argument(\"--since\", required=True, help=\"LAND stamp, ISO 8601 with timezone\")\n239\t    which = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n240\t    which.add_argument(\"--g6\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"only G6 (real loss)\")\n241\t    which.add_argument(\"--g7\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"only G7 (would-log / append failed)\")\n242\t    ap.add_argument(\"--project\", help=\"slug input for the resolver (default: CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR / cwd)\")\n243\t    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n244\t    rep: Dict[str, object] = {}\n245\t    try:\n246\t        since = ss.parse_iso_utc(args.since)\n247\t        family, state = ss.resolve_dirs(args.project)\n248\t        fam = ss.ReadOnlyDir(family)\n249\t        try:\n250\t            if not args.g7:\n251\t                st = ss.ReadOnlyDir(state)\n252\t                try:\n253\t                    rep[\"g6\"] = g6(fam, st, ss.to_ns(since))\n254\t                finally:\n255\t                    st.close()\n256\t            if not args.g6:\n257\t                rep[\"g7\"] = g7(fam, since)\n258\t        finally:\n259\t            fam.close()\n260\t    except (ss.Refused, ValueError, OSError) as e:\n261\t        sys.stderr.write(\"check-audit-real-loss: %s: %s\\n\" % (type(e).__name__, e))\n262\t        return 2\n263\t    rep.update(since=since.isoformat(), state_dir=str(state))\n264\t    red = bool(rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"lost\")) or bool(rep.get(\"g7\", {}).get(\"G7\"))\n265\t    rep[\"red\"] = red\n266\t    rep[\"attention\"] = []\n267\t    if rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"journal_malformed_lines\"):\n268\t        rep[\"attention\"].append(\"g6_journal_malformed_lines\")\n269\t    if rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"malformed_record_id_files\"):\n270\t        rep[\"attention\"].append(\"g6_malformed_record_id_files\")\n271\t    print(json.dumps(rep, indent=1, sort_keys=True))\n272\t    return 1 if red else (2 if rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"inconclusive\") else 0)\n273\t\n274\t\n275\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n276\t    sys.exit(main())\n277\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383b699d-3190-4c1b-a4de-9afabb13d7c6","uuid":"57616024-6b31-47b4-9cd4-940a4cabcf7a","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:28:03.341Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/check-audit-real-loss.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"check-audit-real-loss.py — G6 (real loss) and G7 (direct-writer loss), read-only.\n\nPLAN-194 W2 / ADR-055-AMEND-4 §8.2. Runs outside any hook (LAND V-block,\nnightly, ``/ceo-boot``); ``--since`` is the LAND stamp.\n\n**G6.** A ``record_id`` with a ``commit`` envelope in a per-PID journal (or the\naggregate journal) and ``wall_ns >= since`` that is neither in the canonical log\nnor in a rotated archive nor in any spool-side file. Reading order, so a record\nin transit is never called lost: (0) the journals; (1) a FRESH listing of the\nspool side — active spools and ``.draining.*`` (PENDING) and the quarantine\nfiles ``.malformed.*``/``.quarantined.*``/``.test-origin.*``/``.corrupt-header.*``\n(QUARANTINED, never lost); (2) the canonical log through one descriptor; (3) the\nrotated archives, listed after it. A record only moves spool -> log (append\nbefore unlink) and rotation renames the log. Log lines count by their TOP-LEVEL\n``record_id``; a spool-side line that is not JSON (quarantine) is searched with\n``_RID_RX``. Lower bound: a ``commit`` that never left the in-memory journal\nbuffer, one whose journal compaction removed, or one TRUNCATED on disk (it is a\nline that does not parse: only ``journal_malformed_lines`` sees it) is invisible.\nHence ``attention`` (below).\n\nA pass of (1)-(3) is STABLE only if every listed spool-side file and archive was\nread (none vanished between the listing and the read — a drain renames active\n-> ``.draining``, a quarantine ``.draining`` -> ``.malformed``, a split writes a\nnew ``.draining``) AND no ``.draining``/quarantine name shows up in a re-listing\nthat the first listing missed (a rename caught mid-``readdir``). Where a record\nIS seen counts in any pass; its ABSENCE counts only in stable passes. A loss is\nreported only after TWO stable passes; if ``MAX_PASSES`` run out first the\ncandidates are ``unresolved`` and G6 is ``inconclusive`` (exit 2, never \"lost\").\nA journal that vanishes is counted apart (``journals_vanished``): it can only\nshrink the commit set, never create a loss.\n\n**G7.** ``audit_log`` lines (``[ts]`` stamp) ``lock timeout (stale?)  would-log=``\nor ``append failed:`` in ``audit-log.errors`` stamped at or after ``since``. The\nline parser reads BOTH stamp formats (``[AAAA-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ] ...`` of\n``audit_log`` and ``AAAA-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ <writer>: ...``, §4.8 — the bare stamp is\nshared by ``spool_writer``, ``audit_emit`` and ``check_budget``, so a class is\nkeyed on the WRITER too) and also reports, never as G7, the ``STARVED`` lines (G8\n``(exit)`` and the AMEND-3 opportunistic one) and ``drain canonical lock timeout``\n(G2). A line with no stamp, or an impossible date, is counted as ``unparsed``.\nThe ``STARVED (exit)`` text is the W2 form pinned by §4.3; until the W2 lands it\nexists only in the amendment and in the test fixture, so G8 reads 0 by design.\n\n``attention`` lists what the caller (``/ceo-boot``, nightly) must surface even\nthough the exit code ignores it: ``g6_journal_malformed_lines`` — at least one\njournal line that does not parse, e.g. a truncated ``commit``, whose record G6\ncannot follow.\n\nNames, resolver, refusal, streaming and read-only discipline come from\n``audit_spool_state.py``. Exit: 0 clean; 1 G6 loss > 0 or G7 > 0; 2 usage,\nrefusal, unreadable input, or G6 inconclusive with nothing red. Stdlib only,\nPython >= 3.9.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n\n# These entries are read-only diagnostics.  Set this before loading the local\n# verifier so a normal CLI invocation cannot create a cache beside its source.\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n\nif str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport audit_spool_state as ss  # noqa: E402\n\nRE_QUARANTINE = (r\"audit-spool\\.([1-9][0-9]{0,9})\"\n                 r\"\\.(?:malformed|quarantined|test-origin|corrupt-header)\\.([0-9a-f]{8})\")\n_QUARANTINE_RX = re.compile(RE_QUARANTINE, re.ASCII)\nAGGREGATE_JOURNAL = \"audit-pending.journal\"\nERRORS_FILE = \"audit-log.errors\"\nMAX_PASSES = 8\n_RID_RX = re.compile(rb'\"record_id\"\\s*:\\s*\"([0-9a-f]{32})\"')\n_STAMP = r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}Z\"\nRE_ERR_LINE = r\"(?:\\[(%s)\\] |(%s) ([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*): )(.*)\" % (_STAMP, _STAMP)\n_ERR_LINE_RX = re.compile(RE_ERR_LINE, re.ASCII)\n# (class, source, message prefix); first match wins. Only the g7_* classes are G7.\nERR_CLASSES = (\n    (\"g7_would_log\", \"audit_log\", \"lock timeout (stale?)  would-log=\"),\n    (\"g7_append_failed\", \"audit_log\", \"append failed:\"),\n    # PLAN-194 W2.1: this text exists only in ADR-055-AMEND-4 §4.3 until W2.1 ships\n    # its producer; then the G7 control drops the typed line for the real producer.\n    (\"g8_starved_exit\", \"spool_writer\", \"drain canonical lock STARVED (exit)\"),\n    (\"starved_opportunistic\", \"spool_writer\", \"drain canonical lock STARVED:\"),\n    (\"g2_canonical_lock_timeout\", \"spool_writer\", \"drain canonical lock timeout\"),\n)\n\n\ndef _is_int(v: object) -> bool:\n    return isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool)\n\n\ndef record_ids(lines: Iterable[bytes], top_level_only: bool, wanted: Set[str],\n               malformed_files: Optional[Set[str]] = None, source: str = \"\") -> Set[str]:\n    \"\"\"The ``wanted`` ids among ``lines`` (memory follows the candidates, not the log).\"\"\"\n    out: Set[str] = set()\n    for line in lines:\n        if b'\"record_id\"' not in line:\n            continue\n        try:\n            e = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError:\n            if not top_level_only:\n                out.update(r for r in (m.decode(\"ascii\") for m in _RID_RX.findall(line))\n                           if r in wanted)\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(e, dict) or \"record_id\" not in e:\n            continue\n        rid = e[\"record_id\"]\n        if not isinstance(rid, str):\n            if malformed_files is not None:\n                malformed_files.add(source)\n            continue\n        if rid in wanted:\n            out.add(rid)\n    return out\n\n\ndef journal_commits(st: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since_ns: int) -> Tuple[Set[str], int, int]:\n    commits: Set[str] = set()\n    malformed = 0\n    vanished: List[str] = []\n    for name in st.names():\n        if name != AGGREGATE_JOURNAL and not ss.NAME_PATTERNS[\"journal\"].fullmatch(name):\n            continue\n        for line in ss.listed_lines(st, name, vanished):\n            if not line.strip():\n                continue\n            try:\n                env = json.loads(line)\n            except ValueError:\n                malformed += 1\n                continue\n            if (isinstance(env, dict) and env.get(\"op\") == \"commit\"\n                    and isinstance(env.get(\"record_id\"), str)\n                    and _is_int(env.get(\"wall_ns\")) and env[\"wall_ns\"] >= since_ns):\n                commits.add(env[\"record_id\"])\n    return commits, malformed, len(vanished)\n\n\ndef _spool_side(name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    kind, _ = ss.classify(name)\n    if kind in (\"active_spool\", \"draining\"):\n        return \"pending\"\n    return \"quarantined\" if _QUARANTINE_RX.fullmatch(name) else None\n\n\ndef snapshot(fam: ss.ReadOnlyDir, st: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since_ns: int,\n             wanted: Set[str]) -> Dict[str, Set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Steps (1)-(3) of the reading order, from fresh listings; ``unstable`` names\n    the files that vanished before their read and the rename targets that appeared.\"\"\"\n    snap: Dict[str, Set[str]] = {\n        \"pending\": set(), \"quarantined\": set(), \"logged\": set(),\n        \"malformed_record_id_files\": set(),\n    }\n    vanished: List[str] = []\n    listed = {n: k for n, k in ((n, _spool_side(n)) for n in st.names()) if k}\n    for name in sorted(listed):\n        snap[listed[name]] |= record_ids(\n            ss.listed_lines(st, name, vanished), False, wanted,\n            snap[\"malformed_record_id_files\"], name,\n        )\n    for name, lines in ss.read_logs(fam, since_ns, vanished):\n        snap[\"logged\"] |= record_ids(\n            lines, True, wanted, snap[\"malformed_record_id_files\"], name,\n        )\n    appeared = [n for n in st.names() if n not in listed and _spool_side(n)\n                and ss.classify(n)[0] != \"active_spool\"]  # never a rename target\n    snap[\"unstable\"] = set(vanished) | set(appeared)\n    return snap\n\n\ndef g6(fam: ss.ReadOnlyDir, st: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since_ns: int) -> Dict[str, object]:\n    commits, malformed, journals_vanished = journal_commits(st, since_ns)\n    lost = set(commits)\n    pending: Set[str] = set()\n    quarantined: Set[str] = set()\n    unstable: List[str] = []\n    malformed_record_id_files: Set[str] = set()\n    passes = stable = 0\n    while lost and stable < 2 and passes < MAX_PASSES:\n        passes += 1\n        snap = snapshot(fam, st, since_ns, lost)\n        malformed_record_id_files |= snap.get(\"malformed_record_id_files\", set())\n        lost -= snap[\"logged\"]\n        quarantined |= lost & snap[\"quarantined\"]\n        lost -= snap[\"quarantined\"]\n        pending |= lost & snap[\"pending\"]\n        lost -= snap[\"pending\"]\n        if snap[\"unstable\"]:\n            unstable = sorted(snap[\"unstable\"])\n        else:\n            stable += 1\n    inconclusive = bool(lost) and stable < 2\n    ids = sorted(lost)[:50]\n    return {\"commits\": len(commits), \"pending\": len(pending), \"quarantined\": len(quarantined),\n            \"lost\": 0 if inconclusive else len(lost), \"lost_record_ids\": [] if inconclusive else ids,\n            \"inconclusive\": inconclusive, \"unresolved\": len(lost) if inconclusive else 0,\n            \"unresolved_record_ids\": ids if inconclusive else [], \"passes\": passes,\n            \"stable_passes\": stable, \"last_unstable\": unstable[:20],\n            \"journals_vanished\": journals_vanished, \"journal_malformed_lines\": malformed,\n            \"malformed_record_id_files\": sorted(malformed_record_id_files)[:50]}\n\n\ndef g7(fam: ss.ReadOnlyDir, since: datetime) -> Dict[str, object]:\n    counts = {cls: 0 for cls, _, _ in ERR_CLASSES}\n    counts.update(lines_in_window=0, unparsed=0)\n    for line in ss.listed_lines(fam, ERRORS_FILE, []):\n        raw = line.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\").rstrip(\"\\n\")\n        m = _ERR_LINE_RX.fullmatch(raw)\n        try:\n            ts = datetime.strptime(m.group(1) or m.group(2), \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\") if m else None\n        except ValueError:\n            ts = None\n        if ts is None:\n            counts[\"unparsed\"] += 1 if raw else 0\n            continue\n        if ts.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) < since:\n            continue\n        counts[\"lines_in_window\"] += 1\n        source = \"audit_log\" if m.group(1) else m.group(3)\n        for cls, src, prefix in ERR_CLASSES:\n            if src == source and m.group(4).startswith(prefix):\n                counts[cls] += 1\n                break\n    counts[\"G7\"] = counts[\"g7_would_log\"] + counts[\"g7_append_failed\"]\n    return counts\n\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"check-audit-real-loss.py\", description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n    ap.add_argument(\"--since\", required=True, help=\"LAND stamp, ISO 8601 with timezone\")\n    which = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()\n    which.add_argument(\"--g6\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"only G6 (real loss)\")\n    which.add_argument(\"--g7\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"only G7 (would-log / append failed)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--project\", help=\"slug input for the resolver (default: CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR / cwd)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n    rep: Dict[str, object] = {}\n    try:\n        since = ss.parse_iso_utc(args.since)\n        family, state = ss.resolve_dirs(args.project)\n        fam = ss.ReadOnlyDir(family)\n        try:\n            if not args.g7:\n                st = ss.ReadOnlyDir(state)\n                try:\n                    rep[\"g6\"] = g6(fam, st, ss.to_ns(since))\n                finally:\n                    st.close()\n            if not args.g6:\n                rep[\"g7\"] = g7(fam, since)\n        finally:\n            fam.close()\n    except (ss.Refused, ValueError, OSError) as e:\n        sys.stderr.write(\"check-audit-real-loss: %s: %s\\n\" % (type(e).__name__, e))\n        return 2\n    rep.update(since=since.isoformat(), state_dir=str(state))\n    red = bool(rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"lost\")) or bool(rep.get(\"g7\", {}).get(\"G7\"))\n    rep[\"red\"] = red\n    rep[\"attention\"] = []\n    if rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"journal_malformed_lines\"):\n        rep[\"attention\"].append(\"g6_journal_malformed_lines\")\n    if rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"malformed_record_id_files\"):\n        rep[\"attention\"].append(\"g6_malformed_record_id_files\")\n    print(json.dumps(rep, indent=1, sort_keys=True))\n    return 1 if red else (2 if rep.get(\"g6\", {}).get(\"inconclusive\") else 0)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":277,"startLine":1,"totalLines":277}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UGPiQ5pqjhoUyHgBzY7vR6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
