{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1QcVRFo3g1er8k9jebu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Payload 27/32: no P0, no new P1, ten P2 follow-ups.** The declared conditions that touch this payload (3(b), 3(c), 7) hold against the code.\n\n**Declared conditions checked against the code (all hold)**\n- **Condition 3(b).** `check-audit-real-loss.py` no longer crashes on a `record_id` that isn't text. `record_ids()` (lines 113-119) adds the file to `malformed_record_id_files`. `g6()` reports it (line 208) and `main()` lists `g6_malformed_record_id_files` under `attention` (lines 269-270).\n- **Condition 3(c).** Both read-only checkers stop writing bytecode before loading their helpers. In `check-audit-real-loss.py`, line 67 sets `sys.dont_write_bytecode = True` before `import audit_spool_state` at line 71. In `audit_spool_state.py`, line 62 comes before `from _lib import runtime_paths` at line 69.\n- **Condition 7.**\n  - `ceo-cost-transcripts.py` (lines 248-252) and `ceo-boot.py` (lines 114-116) are now thin entry points over `_lib/_cost_transcripts_parts` and `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts`.\n  - `ceo-boot`'s `main()` was moved complete to `_ceo_boot_parts/lessons_cli.py:132-253`. That includes the task-candidate markers and the `ceo_boot_emitted` audit event on both the cached and uncached paths.\n  - Neither parts package is a kernel path, which fits condition 5: neither script is a kernel entry point.\n  - The kernel loaders (`canonical_edit`, `agent_spawn`, `_audit_emit_parts`, `_pair_rail_parts`) only re-bind top-level functions, so the P2 below does not reach any governance hook.\n- **CHANGELOG restore claims.** These match the code, except for the trailing-slash case in P2-4.\n\n**Other checks**\n- **Python.** Standard library only. Nothing beyond Python 3.9 syntax in the parts, the archive validator, the hooks-executable checker or the lint.\n- **Fail direction is correct.**\n  - The hooks-executable checker exits 2 on settings it cannot parse (fails closed).\n  - If the transcripts instrument fails to import, `ceo-cost.py`'s loader catches it and shows a note (fails open).\n  - Restore refuses links, traversal paths, key files and duplicate names before writing anything. It extracts only accepted members into a fresh temp directory, opening each with `O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW`.\n\n**NEW FINDINGS (annex)**\nNone at P1.\n\n**P2 follow-ups**\n\n1. **Debug output of the cost-transcripts objects crashes.** `.claude/hooks/_lib/_cost_transcripts_parts/__init__.py:54-56`\n   - **Cause:** `install()` re-binds every class-dict function whose module matches the part module to the entry script's globals. That includes the `__repr__` wrapper that dataclasses generates, because `functools.wraps` copies its module name. The wrapper looks up `_thread` (on Python 3.13+, `get_ident`) from the dataclasses module's globals, and the entry script has neither.\n   - **Effect:** `repr()`, `str()` or `print()` of any `UsageRecord`, `ScanCounters`, `PricingResult` or `Priced` built through the entry script raises `NameError`. The old single-file module did not.\n   - **Impact:** `transcript_rollup()` returns `pricing_result` and `counters` objects, so anyone who prints that dict, or a test assertion message, hits it. No shipped path reprs these objects: `collect()` returns plain data.\n   - **Fix:** only re-bind methods whose `__code__.co_filename` is the part's own file. Equivalently, skip functions that have `__wrapped__`, or skip dataclass-generated methods altogether.\n\n2. **Dead duplicate of a Tier-A check.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120`\n   - The entry script redefines `check_tier_a_spec_version_drift` after `install()` has run. `TIER_A_CHECKS` (`_ceo_boot_parts/scheduled_cache.py:376`) has already captured the version from `model_persona.py:6`.\n   - The two bodies match today, so behaviour is unchanged. But the copy a reader sees in the entry script is dead: editing it changes nothing at runtime.\n   - **Fix:** delete the copy in the entry script.\n\n3. **Stale docstring in the cost-transcripts entry script.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py:32, 208, 241-243`\n   - Line 32 says `_EMBEDDED_PRICING` is \"below\"; it now lives in `_cost_transcripts_parts/pricing.py`.\n   - Line 208 says \"this script writes nothing\". It now imports seven helper modules with bytecode writing still on, so it writes `__pycache__` beside them (the same class as condition 3(c)).\n   - **Fix:** correct the pointer, and set `sys.dont_write_bytecode` before the imports or soften the claim.\n\n4. **A link with a trailing slash passes as the restore destination.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:175-176`\n   - `--dest /path/link/` makes `[ -L ]` false, so the link is accepted and resolved to its target. The CHANGELOG says restore \"refuses a link ... as the destination\".\n   - **Fix:** strip trailing slashes from `raw` before the tests.\n\n5. **Documented disaster-recovery path now fails on a new machine.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:182-184`\n   - `_physical_dest` requires the destination's parent to already exist and not be a link.\n   - On a new machine without `~/.claude/projects`, the recovery in `DISASTER-RECOVERY.md` Scenario D now exits 2. The old script created the directory with `mkdir -p`.\n   - On macOS, `--dest /tmp/x` is also refused, because `/tmp` is a link.\n   - It fails closed with a named error, so no data is at risk.\n   - **Fix:** check the nearest existing ancestor for links, then `mkdir -p`. Or document the `mkdir` step.\n\n6. **Gap between the check and the copy.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:292` vs `302-351`\n   - The symlink pre-check runs before the confirmation prompt, which can wait indefinitely. `cp` then follows any link planted in that window.\n   - **Fix:** run `_preflight_targets` again after the prompt, just before copying.\n\n7. **`CDPATH` can corrupt the destination path.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:179, 185`\n   - `cd -P` inside `$(...)` prints the directory when an exported `CDPATH` resolves a relative `--dest`. `DEST` then holds two lines, and `mkdir` and `cp` write to a stray path.\n   - **Fix:** use `CDPATH= cd -P`, or `unset CDPATH` at the top of the script.\n\n8. **Restore messages say less than before.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:243-245, 302-304`\n   - The preview listing now stops at 50 lines without the old \"use tar tzf\" hint, while the usage text (lines 46-49) promises \"every file\". It also lists AppleDouble members that are never written.\n   - The confirmation prompt no longer names the files it will overwrite under the current directory for `--restore-plans` and `--restore-agent-metrics`.\n   - **Fix:** restore the truncation hint and list the optional targets in the prompt.\n\n9. **Possible endless loop in the link check.** `.claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:257-263`\n   - `_refuse_link_ancestors` stops only on string equality with `$stop`. With `DEST=/` or the current directory at `/`, GNU `dirname //x` gives `//` and the loop never ends. This is a degenerate case.\n   - **Fix:** also stop when the path is `/` or `//`.\n\n10. **Unlisted hook types turn the harness gate red.** `.claude/scripts/check-active-hooks-executable.py:165-166`\n    - Any hook `type` outside the five-entry table exits 2, which `check_harness_config` reports as RED in `/ceo-boot`.\n    - This is advisory only and never blocks a session. But a hook type the Claude Code loader accepts and the table lacks would show a false RED for adopters.\n    - **Fix:** keep the table in step with the loader, or downgrade unknown types to a named warning.\n\n11. **Docstring omits the new `attention` item.** `.claude/scripts/check-audit-real-loss.py:44-47`\n    - The `attention` paragraph names only `g6_journal_malformed_lines`; the new `g6_malformed_record_id_files` (line 270) is undocumented.\n    - **Fix:** add it to the docstring.\n\n**Nothing to report in the rest of the payload**\n- **Waivers file:** valid JSON; the 47 new waivers are pinned to the content hash of already-run historical files.\n- **Ceremony-script lint:** the new R9 and R10 rules run only in CI and the maintainer pre-commit hook, never in an adopter session.\n- **Audit-registry coverage check:** it now also reads `emit_*` definitions in `_audit_emit_parts`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3526,"cache_read_input_tokens":229321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3526},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"383b699d-3190-4c1b-a4de-9afabb13d7c6","uuid":"cfb55151-f5fc-4ab6-8e82-a09cfafd1220","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:35:13.694Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1QcUzD9tzaNN54iLgsh"}
