st_transcripts_parts/pricing.py.\n  - It says \"this script writes nothing\". It now imports seven helper modules without sys.dont_write_bytecode, so it writes __pycache__ beside them (same class as condition 3(c)).\n  - An empty \"Pricing tables\" header is left behind.\n  - Fix: correct the pointer, and set dont_write_bytecode before the imports or soften the claim.\nP2-4  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:175-176\n  - `--dest /path/link/` with a trailing slash makes `[ -L ]` false, so the link is accepted and resolved to its target. CHANGELOG says restore \"refuses a link ... as the destination\".\n  - Fix: strip trailing slashes from raw before the tests.\nP2-5  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:182-184\n  - _physical_dest requires an existing, non-link parent. DISASTER-RECOVERY.md Scenario D (new machine, no ~/.claude/projects) now exits 2 where the old script ran mkdir -p.\n  - On macOS, `--dest /tmp/x` is refused because /tmp is a symlink.\n  - Fails closed with a named error; no data at risk.\n  - Fix: check link-freedom on the nearest existing ancestor, then mkdir -p; or document the mkdir step.\nP2-6  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:292 vs :302-351\n  - The link pre-check runs before the confirmation prompt, which can wait indefinitely. cp follows a link planted in that window.\n  - Fix: re-run _preflight_targets after the prompt, immediately before copying.\nP2-7  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:179, :185\n  - `cd -P` inside $(...) prints the directory when an exported CDPATH resolves a relative --dest. DEST then holds two lines, and mkdir/cp write to a stray path.\n  - Fix: `CDPATH= cd -P`, or unset CDPATH at the top of the script.\nP2-8  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:243-245, :302-304\n  - The preview listing is cut at 50 lines without the old \"use tar tzf\" hint, while usage (:46-49) promises \"every file\". It also lists AppleDouble members that are never written.\n  - The confirmation prompt no longer names the CWD targets of --restore-plans and --restore-