ed built through the entry script raises NameError. The old single-file module did not.\n  - Scenario: printing transcript_rollup()'s result (it returns the pricing_result and counters objects), or a pytest/unittest failure message on these objects, crashes. No shipped path reprs them: collect() returns plain data.\n  - Fix: re-bind only methods whose __code__.co_filename is the part's own file (equivalently, skip functions with __wrapped__), or skip dataclass-generated methods entirely.\nP2-2  .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:120\n  - The entry script redefines check_tier_a_spec_version_drift after install(). TIER_A_CHECKS (_ceo_boot_parts/scheduled_cache.py:376) already captured the copy from model_persona.py:6.\n  - The bodies match today, but the visible copy is dead: editing it changes nothing at runtime.\n  - Fix: delete the entry-script copy.\nP2-3  .claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py:32, :208, :241-243 (honesty)\n  - The docstring says _EMBEDDED_PRICING is \"below\"; it now lives in _cost_transcripts_parts/pricing.py.\n  - It says \"this script writes nothing\". It now imports seven helper modules without sys.dont_write_bytecode, so it writes __pycache__ beside them (same class as condition 3(c)).\n  - An empty \"Pricing tables\" header is left behind.\n  - Fix: correct the pointer, and set dont_write_bytecode before the imports or soften the claim.\nP2-4  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:175-176\n  - `--dest /path/link/` with a trailing slash makes `[ -L ]` false, so the link is accepted and resolved to its target. CHANGELOG says restore \"refuses a link ... as the destination\".\n  - Fix: strip trailing slashes from raw before the tests.\nP2-5  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:182-184\n  - _physical_dest requires an existing, non-link parent. DISASTER-RECOVERY.md Scenario D (new machine, no ~/.claude/projects) now exits 2 where the old script ran mkdir -p.\n  - On macOS, `--dest /tmp/x` is refused because /tmp is a symlink.\n  - Fails closed with a named error; no data at risk.\n  - Fix: check link-freedom on the nearest existing ancestor, then mkdir -p; or document the mkdir step.\nP2-6  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:292 vs :302-351\n  - The link pre-check runs before the confirmation prompt, which can wait indefinitely. cp follows a link planted in that window.\n  - Fix: re-run _preflight_targets after the prompt, immediately before copying.\nP2-7  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:179, :185\n  - `cd -P` inside $(...) prints the directory when an exported CDPATH resolves a relative --dest. DEST then holds two lines, and mkdir/cp write to a stray path.\n  - Fix: `CDPATH= cd -P`, or unset CDPATH at the top of the script.\nP2-8  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:243-245, :302-304\n  - The preview listing is cut at 50 lines without the old \"use tar tzf\" hint, while usage (:46-49) promises \"every file\". It also lists AppleDouble members that are never written.\n  - The confirmation prompt no longer names the CWD targets of --restore-plans and --restore-agent-metrics.\n  - Fix: restore the truncation hint and list the optional targets in the prompt.\nP2-9  .claude/scripts/ceo-restore.sh:257-263\n  - _refuse_link_ancestors stops only on string equality with stop. With DEST=/ or CWD=/, GNU `dirname //x` yields `//` and the loop never ends (degenerate case).\n  - Fix: also break when path is / or //.\nP2-10  .claude/scripts/check-active-hooks-executable.py:165-166\n  - Any hook type outside the five-entry table exits 2, which check_harness_config shows as RED in /ceo-boot.\n  - Advisory only, never blocks a session. But a type the Claude Code loader accepts and the table lacks would give adopters a false RED.\n  - Fix: keep the table in step with the loader, or downgrade unknown types to a named warning.\nP2-11  .claude/scripts/check-audit-real-loss.py:44-47\n  - The docstring's attention paragraph names only g6_journal_malformed_lines; the new g6_malformed_record_id_files (:270) is undocumented.\n  - Fix: add it.\n\nNOTHING TO REPORT\n- ceremony-lint-waivers.json: valid JSON; 47 content-sha-pinned waivers for already-run historical files.\n- check-ceremony-script.py: R9 and R10 run only in CI and the maintainer pre-commit hook, never in an adopter session.\n- check-audit-registry-coverage.py: now also reads emit_* definitions from _audit_emit_parts.","decision":"GO","sentence":"The declared conditions this payload touches (3(b), 3(c), 7) hold against the code and no P0 was found; the moved-code repr regression in the cost-transcripts loader and the restore-script edge cases do not affect governance hooks or adopter sessions, so they are listed as P2 follow-ups."},"ttft_ms":4731,"type":"result","duration_ms":660421,"uuid":"382bef1a-2be9-4272-b359-30a27ce4a396","ttft_stream_ms":2973,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":2973,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":80,"outputTokens":59755,"cacheReadInputTokens":6631838,"cacheCreationInputTokens":228374,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.3487796,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":43163,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":228374,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-20T15:54:23.997Z"}
